course: dictionary
lesson: 8514
title: Satisfaction: more than a happy feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Satisfaction is the good, pleased feeling you get when you have done something well or got what you wanted. Finishing a hard puzzle can bring it. You can often find the meaning from the words around it, so check the clues first.
explain: «All Nature joining in a chorus of approval to the song of self-praise that his own heart was singing to him, he almost danced along the road in his satisfaction and conceit.» Everything seems to cheer him on, and he dances along the road. So satisfaction here is a proud, happy glow, and conceit is the too-proud part of it.
explain: «Badger and the Rat kept staring at each other with their mouths open; and this gave him the greatest satisfaction.» Their open mouths show they are amazed, and that pleased him. Try the swap test: «this gave him the greatest pleasure» still makes sense, so satisfaction means a deep, pleased feeling.
explain: Satisfaction has other meanings too. «Customer satisfaction» means how pleased shoppers are. «To my satisfaction» means proof that removes all doubt. Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning.
fact: Satisfaction is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so you say «great satisfaction», not «a satisfaction».
fact: Satisfaction means the good feeling you get when you have done something well or got what you wanted.
fact: «Customer satisfaction» means how pleased customers are with a shop, a service or a product.
fact: «To my satisfaction» is formal and means proof that leaves no doubt.
fact: Satisfaction can also mean making up for a wrong, such as an apology or a payment. This is a formal use.
exercise: «...in his satisfaction and conceit.» What does satisfaction mean here? | Being sorry for a wrong | *A proud, happy feeling | A payment for damage | Doubt about the road
exercise: A shop asks, «Please rate your customer satisfaction.» What is being measured? | How quickly the shop was built | How loudly the customers talk | How many shoes are in stock | *How pleased customers are with the shop
exercise: Ben finishes his model boat and feels a warm glow. Which word fits best? | Panic | *Satisfaction | Boredom | Confusion
test: «...this gave him the greatest satisfaction.» Which word could replace satisfaction without changing the meaning much? | Hunger | Anger | *Pleasure | Fear
test: The teacher says the answer is correct «to my satisfaction». What does this mean? | She has lost her pen | *She is sure the answer is right, with no doubt left | She is hungry and wants lunch | She is cross that you were wrong
exam: Which sentence uses satisfaction correctly? | Satisfaction jumped over the fence and ran home. | He ate satisfaction for lunch on Tuesday. | The satisfaction was a big brown dog in the garden. | *She felt great satisfaction when her model boat floated.
